GN hands the rust Bazel build a target platform only on mac. For Android it
passes nothing, so Bazel builds the rust png codec for the host (linux x86_64)
and the archive cannot link into an arm64 binary.

This adds the arm64 case only. arm32 would also need armv7-linux-androideabi
in MODULE.bazel (skia-152-bazel-rust-android-triples.patch adds arm64 alone),
and there is no Android x64 platform in bazel/platform. Builds without rust
are not affected.

Checked on Skia 152 (0873ec164a) under WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 with NDK r27d:
`ninja skia` for target_os="android" target_cpu="arm64" with
skia_use_rust_png_decode=true, and a probe executable links against the result
with -Wl,--allow-multiple-definition (what rust_ffi_libs_config in BUILD.gn
already asks for).

diff --git a/BUILD.gn b/BUILD.gn
index df31ad6389..4a59692df5 100644
--- a/BUILD.gn
+++ b/BUILD.gn
@@ -1372,6 +1372,9 @@ if (is_mac) {
     bazel_args += [ "--platforms=//bazel/platform:mac_x64_hermetic" ]
   }
 }
+if (is_android && target_cpu == "arm64") {
+  bazel_args += [ "--platforms=//bazel/platform:android_arm64" ]
+}
 if (is_debug) {
   bazel_args += [ "--compilation_mode=dbg" ]
 } else {
